  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Hyperfine’s core portable MRI business is showing accelerating commercial traction, with unit sales rising sharply and gross margins expanding meaningfully as the company scales. The Swoop system appears to be gaining adoption, likely supported by growing clinician acceptance and a favorable shift toward point-of-care imaging. The environment remains competitive, but demand momentum is clearly positive, and the company’s ability to sustain this volume growth while improving profitability on each device signals an improving market position.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a disciplined turnaround, simultaneously driving top-line growth and tightening operational efficiency. Actions include materially reducing R&D spend while keeping selling and administrative costs flat, resulting in a narrower net loss and lower cash burn. This cost-conscious yet growth-oriented posture is rebuilding credibility. Analyst sentiment reflects cautious optimism, with some firms upgrading targets to reflect the improving trajectory, though the overall consensus remains tempered.",
